@model ApplyStatus
@*
    The apply button and the restart banner, or nothing (D43, D104). They are in the navbar rather
    than on each page because "Asterisk is running config older than the database" is true of the
    whole system, not of the page you happen to be looking at, and because a control that is only
    there when there is something to do needs no explaining.

    The banner stays until a restart actually happens: an apply that wrote a startup-only file
    offers the restart straight away, and this is where an admin who said "not now" comes back to
    it (D33, D104).
*@
@if (Model.RestartRequired)
{
    <span class="badge text-bg-warning me-2" title="An apply wrote a file Asterisk only reads when it starts, so it is still running the config it started with.">
        Asterisk restart required
    </span>
    <button type="button" class="btn btn-warning me-2" onclick="pbx.restartAsterisk(this)"
            title="Restarts Asterisk so it reads the files it only reads at startup. This drops any calls in progress.">
        Restart Asterisk
    </button>
}
@if (Model.ConfigPending)
{
    <button type="button" class="btn btn-danger" onclick="pbx.applyConfig(this)"
            title="The configuration has changed since the last apply. This writes it to Asterisk and reloads what changed.">
        Apply config
    </button>
}
